In .NET 10 (and late .NET 9), Android's `SOFT_INPUT_ADJUST_RESIZE` is fully deprecated. MAUI replaced it with **`KeyboardAutoManagerScroll`**, which is enabled by default and automatically scrolls focused views into view.

For a chat screen, here's what to do:

**1. Ensure auto-scroll is not disabled**

Don't opt out globally. If you previously disabled it, remove:
```csharp
// ❌ Remove this if present
KeyboardAutoManagerScroll.Disconnect();
```

**2. Use a layout that cooperates with the auto-manager**

```xml
<Grid RowDefinitions="*,Auto">
    <CollectionView Grid.Row="0" ItemsSource="{Binding Messages}" />

    <!-- This entry will be scrolled above the keyboard automatically -->
    <HorizontalStackLayout Grid.Row="1" Padding="8">
        <Entry Placeholder="Type a message..." HorizontalOptions="FillAndExpand" />
        <Button Text="Send" />
    </HorizontalStackLayout>
</Grid>
```

**3. If auto-scroll alone isn't enough (common in chat UIs), manually respond to insets on Android:**

In `Platforms/Android/MainActivity.cs`:

```csharp
using AndroidX.Core.View;
using Microsoft.Maui.Controls.Compatibility.Platform.Android;

protected override void OnCreate(Bundle? savedInstanceState)
{
    base.OnCreate(savedInstanceState);

    ViewCompat.SetOnApplyWindowInsetsListener(Window!.DecorView, new InsetsListener(this));
}

private class InsetsListener(Activity activity) : Java.Lang.Object, IOnApplyWindowInsetsListener
{
    public WindowInsetsCompat OnApplyWindowInsets(Android.Views.View v, WindowInsetsCompat insets)
    {
        var imeInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.Ime());
        var navInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.NavigationBars());

        // Bottom padding = keyboard height minus nav bar
        var bottomPadding = Math.Max(imeInsets.Bottom - navInsets.Bottom, 0);

        // Apply to the MAUI content's padding
        if (activity is MauiAppCompatActivity mauiActivity)
        {
            var page = Shell.Current?.CurrentPage ?? Application.Current?.Windows[0].Page;
            if (page != null)
                page.Padding = new Thickness(0, 0, 0, bottomPadding / DeviceDisplay.MainDisplayInfo.Density);
        }

        return ViewCompat.OnApplyWindowInsets(v, insets);
    }
}
```

**4. Ensure edge-to-edge / IME insets are enabled** in `MainActivity`:

```csharp
WindowCompat.SetDecorFitsSystemWindows(Window!, false);
```

**Summary:** `KeyboardAutoManagerScroll` (on by default) handles most cases. For chat UIs where you need the *entire layout* to compress rather than just scroll to a focused field, use the `WindowInsetsCompat.Type.Ime()` listener to dynamically adjust page padding.
